│  1 What does this part of the code do?                             │
│    This is the class definition of ConcurrencyException in         │
│    src/strands/types/exceptions.py. It is a custom exception used  │
│    to signal when concurrent invocations are attempted on the same │
│    Agent instance, which is not safe due to shared internal state. │
│    The exception includes a docstring clarifying the concurrency   │
│    safety concern. Also, agent.py imports this exception and       │
│    raises it in stream_async() when it fails to acquire the        │
│    invocation lock.                                                │
│  2 What is the relationship between this part of the code and the  │
│    bug?                                                            │
│    Currently, the Agent uses a threading.Lock to prevent           │
│    concurrent usage, and if the lock is already held (concurrent   │
│    invocation), it raises this exception. The bug/feature request  │
│    is to optionally allow concurrent invocations by skipping the   │
│    lock or otherwise disabling this throwing behavior. Thus, this  │
│    exception's throwing is the mechanism to be relaxed or bypassed │
│    when a new parameter mode is set.                               │
│  3 Given the issue description, what would be the intended         │
│    behavior of this part of the code?                              │
│    The intended behavior is to conditionally raise this exception  │
│    only if the new concurrent_invocation_mode parameter is set to  │
│    "throw" (the current default). If it is set to                  │
│    "unsafe_reentrant", the code should skip the lock acquisition   │
│    and raising of this exception, enabling concurrent Agent        │
│    invocations without error. The exception definition itself      │
│    remains unchanged (no change needed), but the usage in          │
│    stream_async needs to be made conditional based on the          │
│    concurrency mode.                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
